1. Aim
To implement the Producer-Consumer problem using threads, semaphores and mutex for synchronization.
2. Code Explanation
Step 1: Header Files
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <semaphore.h>
#include <unistd.h>


- stdio.h – Input/output.
- stdlib.h – General functions.
- pthread.h – Thread creation.
- semaphore.h – Semaphore operations.
- unistd.h – sleep() function.
Step 2: Buffer Declaration
#define BUFFER_SIZE 5

int buffer[BUFFER_SIZE];
int in = 0, out = 0;


- BUFFER_SIZE 5 – Buffer can store 5 items.
- buffer[] – Stores produced items.
- in – Position where producer inserts item.
- out – Position where consumer removes item.
Step 3: Semaphore and Mutex
sem_t empty;
sem_t full;

pthread_mutex_t mutex;


- empty – Counts empty spaces.
- full – Counts filled spaces.
- mutex – Protects shared buffer from simultaneous access.
Step 4: Producer Function
for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++)
{
    item = i;

    sem_wait(&empty);
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    buffer[in] = item;
    printf("Producer produced: %d\n", item);

    in = (in + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
    sem_post(&full);

    sleep(1);
}


Explanation:
- for loop – Produces 10 items (1 to 10).
- item = i – Assigns item.
- sem_wait(&empty) – Checks for empty space.
- pthread_mutex_lock() – Locks buffer.
- buffer[in] = item – Inserts item.
- in = (in + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE – Moves to next position circularly.
- pthread_mutex_unlock() – Unlocks buffer.
- sem_post(&full) – Increases filled-space count.
- sleep(1) – Waits 1 second.
Step 5: Consumer Function
for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++)
{
    sem_wait(&full);
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    item = buffer[out];

    printf("Consumer consumed: %d\n", item);

    out = (out + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
    sem_post(&empty);

    sleep(2);
}


Explanation:
- sem_wait(&full) – Waits until an item is available.
- pthread_mutex_lock() – Locks buffer.
- item = buffer[out] – Takes item from buffer.
- printf() – Displays consumed item.
- out = (out + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE – Moves to next position.
- pthread_mutex_unlock() – Unlocks buffer.
- sem_post(&empty) – Increases empty-space count.
- sleep(2) – Waits 2 seconds.
Step 6: Main Function
pthread_t producer_thread, consumer_thread;

sem_init(&empty, 0, BUFFER_SIZE);
sem_init(&full, 0, 0);

pthread_mutex_init(&mutex, NULL);


- pthread_t – Declares two threads.
- sem_init(&empty, 0, BUFFER_SIZE) – Initially 5 empty spaces.
- sem_init(&full, 0, 0) – Initially 0 filled spaces.
- pthread_mutex_init() – Initializes mutex.
Step 7: Create Threads
pthread_create(&producer_thread, NULL, producer, NULL);

pthread_create(&consumer_thread, NULL, consumer, NULL);


Creates producer and consumer threads.

Step 8: Wait for Threads
pthread_join(producer_thread, NULL);
pthread_join(consumer_thread, NULL);


Main function waits until both threads finish execution.

Step 9: Destroy Synchronization Objects
sem_destroy(&empty);
sem_destroy(&full);
pthread_mutex_destroy(&mutex);


Destroys semaphores and mutex after execution.

